[v4] toJsonSchema: Preprocess should always take the out type

When using `toJSONSchema` on a schema with preprocess and a transform using the `io: "input"` option will always result in an error.

This is because a preprocess is (as stated in the docs) a wrapper of a z.pipe with transform input and schema output. I don't really see much of an argument for an `io` option with the preprocess case since the LHS is always a transform and the RHS is the schema I want to serialize. However, I always want to take the input of transforms/refines and serialize that way.

Here's a reproducible example:
```ts
import {z} from "zod/v4";

const TestSchema = z.number().transform((val) => 0)
const testJSON = z.toJSONSchema(TestSchema, {io: "input"});

// Success (type: z.ZodPipe<z.ZodNumber, z.ZodTransform<number, number>>)
console.log(testJSON);

const PreprocessSchema = z.preprocess((data) => data, TestSchema);
const preprocessJSON = z.toJSONSchema(PreprocessSchema, {io: "input"});

// Fails because of preprocess (type: z.ZodPipe<z.ZodTransform<unknown, unknown>, z.ZodPipe<z.ZodNumber, z.ZodTransform<number, number>>>)
console.log(preprocessJSON);
```

The way I'd approach this is to check for a preprocess in the [internal parser](https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/blob/main/packages/zod/src/v4/core/to-json-schema.ts#L501-L506) (case is a ZodPipe with a transform on the LHS) and recursively call the internal parser again, ignoring the `io` option here.

This is done in zod-to-openapi: https://github.com/asteasolutions/zod-to-openapi/pull/301
in the following file: https://github.com/asteasolutions/zod-to-openapi/blob/00943e016b62a2a0d62130ea4439ee8d818fec17/src/metadata.ts#L48-L51

Adding this change should make toJSONSchema more approachable to users in my opinion. I'd like to hear @colinhacks thoughts since I'm unsure if there's any custom way to handle this case as well.

