render() throws TypeError given JSX with that generates an empty array

### What version of Hono are you using?

4.11.4 and 4.11.9

### What runtime/platform is your app running on? (with version if possible)

Deno 2.3.2

### What steps can reproduce the bug?

```tsx
import { render } from "hono/jsx/dom";

function App() {
  const tags: string[] = [];
  const terms: string[] = ["hello"];
  return (
    <div>
      {tags.map((x) => <span>{x}</span>)}
      {terms.map((x) => <span>{x}</span>)}
      <input type="text" />
    </div>
  );
}

render(<App />, document.getElementById("root")!);
// TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'children')
```

### What is the expected behavior?

Empty array should render as nothing and the second array should be rendered.

### What do you see instead?

```
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'children')
    at build (render.ts:477)
    typeof node.tag == 'function' ? invokeTag(context, node) : toArray(node.props.children)
```


### Additional information

| Pattern | Result |
|---------|--------|
| `{[].map(...)}` `<input/>` | ✅ works |
| `{["a"].map(...)}` `{[].map(...)}` | ✅ works |
| `{[].map(...)}` `{[].map(...)}` | ❌ crashes |
| `{[].map(...)}` `{["a"].map(...)}` | ❌ crashes |

The error happens in the `build()` function's child-flattening loop in `src/jsx/dom/render.ts`:

```typescript
for (let i = 0; i < children.length; i++) {
  if (Array.isArray(children[i])) {
    children.splice(i, 1, ...(children[i] as Child[]).flat())
  }
  let child = buildNode(children[i])
```

**Suggested fix:**

Add `i--` after splicing so the loop re-examines the same index:

```typescript
for (let i = 0; i < children.length; i++) {
  if (Array.isArray(children[i])) {
    children.splice(i, 1, ...(children[i] as Child[]).flat())
+   if (i >= children.length) break  // empty array removed, nothing replaced
+   i--  // re-examine this index
+   continue
  }
  let child = buildNode(children[i])
```

