  params: Record<string, string>
}
```

However, it might be that each `handler` should have its own `params`, rather than all handlers sharing one `params`.

For instance, in the current pattern, the result is not as expected. (This example uses TrieRouter, because RegExpRouter has another issue #1140)

```ts
app.get('/webhooks/github', async (c, next) => {
  await next()
})

app.get('/webhooks/:service', (c) => {
  return c.text(`service: ${c.req.param('service')}`)
})
```

```
GET /webhooks/github => service: undefined
```

I believe it should return `service: github`. To make this work correctly, we might need a structure like the one below, where `params` are handled per handler.

```ts
interface Result<T> {
  routes: Route<T>[]
}

interface Route<T> {
  handler: T
  params: Record<string, string>
}
```

If we decide to address these issues, it will require significant effort. But, it might be worth doing.

Component children need to be passed as ordinary props because of the absence of `JSX.ElementChildrenAttribute`

The following Hono code produces an error saying `This JSX tag's 'children' prop expects type 'HtmlEscapedString' which requires multiple children, but only a single child was provided. ts(2745)`:

```ts
