feat: Allow making `ssr` conditional on the request

### Describe the feature you'd like to request

Currently, `ssr` is set at at compile time/statically, as a single boolean field on `createTRPCNext`

```ts
export const api = createTRPCNext<AppRouter>({
  config(opts) {
    const { ctx } = opts;

    const link = httpLink({
      url: `${getBaseUrl()}/api/trpc`,
    });

    return {
      links: [
        loggerLink({
          enabled: (opts) =>
            process.env.NODE_ENV === "development" || (opts.direction === "down" && opts.result instanceof Error),
        }),
        link,
      ],
      queryClient,
    };
  },
  ssr: false,
});
```

However, sometimes you want ssr to be conditional - for instance, for all google bot requests, we'd like to SSR the page so that the initial html contains all our meta tags

### Describe the solution you'd like to see

Allow making `ssr` a back, just like config, where you can pull the `NextPageContext`


```ts
export const api = createTRPCNext<AppRouter>({
  config(opts) {
    const { ctx } = opts;

    const link = httpLink({
      url: `${getBaseUrl()}/api/trpc`,
    });

    return {
      links: [
        loggerLink({
          enabled: (opts) =>
            process.env.NODE_ENV === "development" || (opts.direction === "down" && opts.result instanceof Error),
        }),
        link,
      ],
      queryClient,
    };
  },
  ssr(opts){
    const { ctx } = opts;
    const { req } = ctx;
    return req?.headers?.['user-agent']?.includes('googlebot')
  }
});
```

### Describe alternate solutions

We need access to the request. So another solution might be to allow a hook in `utils` to set it at react runtime on the server.

