With `isolate: false`, each file's `vi.mock` factory is never released, so worker memory grows per file

### Describe the bug

With `isolate: false`, every test file's `vi.mock()` factory stays reachable after the file finishes, together with everything the factory closes over. A worker that runs many files therefore grows by the size of each file's mock-factory scope, and on a large jsdom suite the worker eventually dies with `Worker exited unexpectedly`.

Mocking itself behaves correctly: each file sees its own mock. Only the memory is never released. `vi.resetModules()` at the start of each file does not change it. With `isolate: true` the heap stays flat.

In the reproduction, each of 30 test files mocks the same module with a factory that closes over ~10 MB. The heap measured at the start of each file, after a forced GC (`--expose-gc`), on one worker:

| config | heap used at file start (MB) |
| --- | --- |
| `isolate: false` | 19, 28, 38, 47, 57 … 296 (+~9.6 MB per file) |
| `isolate: false` + `vi.resetModules()` per file | 19, 28, 38, 47, 57 … 296 |
| `isolate: true` | 19 for every file |

In a heap snapshot of a real suite, old copies are retained through `EvaluatedModuleNode.meta.mockedModule.factory` (`VitestModuleRunner.evaluatedModules.idToModuleMap`), and through mock configs whose `vi.fn()` keys are themselves reachable from those factories.

#11092 (shipped in 5.0, closing #9492) already stopped `REGISTERED_MOCKS` from pinning every `vi.fn()`. This is the remaining path that keeps earlier files alive when isolation is off; the last comments on #9492 describe the same "nothing gets released under `isolate: false`" symptom.

### Reproduction

https://github.com/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/vitest-isolate-false-mock-retention

`npm install`, then `npm test`; `heap.log` gets one line per file. `RESET=1 npm test` adds `vi.resetModules()`, and `npm test -- --isolate` is the control. The files, inline for convenience:

`package.json`

```json
{ "name": "vitest-isolate-false-mock-retention", "private": true, "type": "module",
  "scripts": { "test": "node --expose-gc node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run" },
  "devDependencies": { "vitest": "5.0.3" } }
```

`vitest.config.ts`

```ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';

export default defineConfig({
  test: { isolate: false, pool: 'threads', maxWorkers: 1, fileParallelism: false, setupFiles: ['./heap.setup.ts'] },
});
```

`heap.setup.ts`

```ts
import { appendFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { beforeAll, vi } from 'vitest';

if (process.env.RESET === '1') vi.resetModules();
beforeAll(() => {
  (globalThis as { gc?: () => void }).gc?.();
  appendFileSync('heap.log', `${Math.round(process.memoryUsage().heapUsed / 1048576)}\n`);
});
```

`dep.ts`

```ts
export const dep = (): string => 'real';
```

`test/t01.test.ts` … `test/t30.test.ts` (identical apart from the name)

```ts
import { expect, test, vi } from 'vitest';
import { dep } from '../dep';

// ~10 MB that only this file's mock factory references.
const { payload } = vi.hoisted(() => ({ payload: Array.from({ length: 1_250_000 }, (_, i) => i) }));
vi.mock('../dep', () => ({ dep: () => String(payload.length) }));

test('sees its own mock', () => {
  expect(dep()).toBe('1250000');
});
```

Expected: the heap stays roughly flat once a file's mocks are no longer registered, as with `isolate: true`.
Actual: it grows by each file's factory scope for the life of the worker.

