Support combining global coverage thresholds with minimum per-file thresholds

### Clear and concise description of the problem

Currently, Vitest forces users to choose between global coverage thresholds and per-file thresholds (`perFile: true`). It is not possible to enforce both simultaneously in a single test run. 

In many real-world projects, teams want to maintain a high overall project coverage (e.g., 80% global average) while simultaneously ensuring that no individual file drops below a certain absolute minimum baseline (e.g., 50% per-file). 

Right now, if we use global thresholds, a single file can have 0% coverage as long as the overall average is high enough. If we use `perFile: true` with 50%, we completely lose the 80% global project requirement. Relying solely on glob patterns grouping doesn't solve this, as it evaluates the grouped files as a whole, not iteratively per file alongside a global check.

### Suggested solution

Introduce a way to define global thresholds and per-file minimums at the same time within the `coverage.thresholds` options. 

A clean approach could be allowing the `perFile` property to accept an object of thresholds instead of just a boolean, or introducing a dedicated `perFileThresholds` key.

Example of how the API could look:

```typescript
export default defineConfig({
  test: {
