Async fixture teardown not awaited

### Describe the bug

I missed something big in https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/pull/4679 and now v1.0.2 doesn't await fixture teardown at all...
I think existing fixture teardown tests were all synchronous, so this bug wasn't caught. Sorry about that.
Here is a quick reproduction:

```tsx
import { describe, vi, expect, afterAll, test } from 'vitest';

describe('repro', () => {
  const trackFn = vi.fn();

  const myTest = test.extend<{ a: string }>({
    a: async ({}, use) => {
      trackFn('setup-sync');
      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 200));
      trackFn('setup-async');
      await use('ok');
      trackFn('teardown-sync');
      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 200));
      trackFn('teardown-async');
    },
  });

  myTest('quick test', ({ a }) => {
    expect(a).toBe('ok');
    expect(trackFn.mock.calls).toEqual([['setup-sync'], ['setup-async']]);
  });

