Child entities with orphanedRowAction with foreign keys as composite primary key are deleted when updated

## Issue Description

### Expected Behavior
Child entities should exist after the `save` operation.

### Actual Behavior
Child entities are updated then deleted when calling `save`.


### Steps to Reproduce


1. Define an entity `Parent` with `OneToMany` relationship to another entity `Child`
3. Entity `Child` has a composite primary key: parent (`Parent`) id + another entity (`OtherEntity`) id
4. Save an object of type `Parent` with at least 1 child of type `Child`.
5. Make changes in one of the `Child` objects and save the parent again.
--> Children will be updated and then deleted (in the end there are no children in the DB), instead of being saved to the DB.

```typescript
@Entity({ name: 'parents' })
export class Parent {
    @PrimaryGeneratedColumn({ unsigned: true })
    id!: number;

    @OneToMany(() => Child, child => child .parent, { cascade: true })
    children!: Child[];
}


@Entity({ name: 'children' })
export class Child {
    @OneToOne(() => OtherEntity)
    @JoinColumn({ name: 'otherEntityId', referencedColumnName: "id" })
    otherEntity!: OtherEntity;

    @PrimaryColumn({ name: "otherEntityId" })
    otherEntityId!: number;  

    @ManyToOne(() => Parent, parent => parent.children, { orphanedRowAction: 'delete' })
    @JoinColumn({ name: "parentId", referencedColumnName: "id" })
    parent!: Parent;

    @PrimaryColumn({ name: "parentId" })
    parentId!: number;    

    @Column({ name: 'order' })
    order!: number; 
}

@Entity({ name: 'otherEntities' })
